 didn't have  those opportunities so me personally I  think it's a big part of my development  philosophy is getting out there and  experiencing your shift content and  knowing what it feels like in your hand  so that you can go hey when that guy on  YouTube said that thing felt like this  you can go oh yeah I know because I felt  it myself and I know it feels like that  so yeah I know it sounds crazy but good  job it makes me feel better about the  products that we put out when we we pay  very close attention to what we're doing  yeah we do what we call retail checks  and it's something that has kind of been  burned into our DNA since we were before  Infinity Ward and never saw from earch  together but we would do retail checks  and look basically what that would mean  is we'd ship piece of content and  immediately the day it come out we'd all  get our retail kits pop our our copy of  the game in and then just immediately  sit down and play it and we would  literally sit down to play to go please  don't break please don't break please  don't break yeah and so you know it's  also one of those gut checks for  yourself to go yeah we pour our heart  and souls into this you know you don't  want to have spent you know the last 45  50 days working you know 15 16 hour days  only to press X and the game not work  right right so it's also just to make  sure that every all of our ducks are in  a row  moving along exactly how we need it and  then then I can actually go to sleep  arrest I guess  just talking about development and then  then launching it when you're done we  can talk about this is out today on ps4  yeah you didn't mention that that out  today post on ps4 can you say when it's  coming elsewhere it'll it'll be coming  in the near future for Xbox one and PC  players right now ps4 players they're  getting to the bread and butter of this  whole experience I hope those guys are  really enjoying it  but PC and Xbox guys don't worry we have  not forgotten about you cont